You see a shaggy, scary beast with saber-sharp teeth on the cover of the book. You skim through the pages and find some information about it:
"...this beast, which travelers called a saber-toothed wolf, is one of the largest predators of Wild Island. It is primarily a nocturnal animal. Tough fur and a thick layer of subcutaneous fat serve as fine armor, capable of stopping a rifle bullet. It is intolerant to loud and shrill sounds and unable to climb a tree, which can save an unlucky wayfarer who encounters this creature."

You close the book and shiver. It's better to steer clear of such a beast...